Browser-based AI inference faces a significant memory constraint. Traditional browser memory limits make running larger open-source models difficult.

@TPN_Labs addressed this by adapting its inference runtime to support 64-bit memory addressing, increasing the browser's working memory ceiling from 4GB to 16GB.

This opens the door to running substantially larger AI models directly in the browser, with inference happening locally rather than through a remote API.

@Gratis_AI makes this capability accessible. Pick a model, let it download, and run it on your own machine.

